    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "INSTAGRAM HISTORICAL BACKFILL\n\nPurpose:\n- Manual workflow for backfilling Instagram social dashboard rows after connecting a new account or after changing the backfill window.\n- Backfills social_accounts, social_media_content, social_media_daily_metrics, and social_account_daily_metrics.\n\nSetup:\n1. Update Pipeline Config values.\n2. Use service-role key only in n8n. Never expose it client-side.\n3. Set date_start/date_end to the period you want to populate. Default is last 30 completed days.\n4. Run manually first and inspect Supabase rows before enabling or duplicating.\n\nImportant limitation:\nInstagram media insights are pulled as current/lifetime snapshots and stored on date_end. Meta does not reliably reconstruct day-by-day historical media insight values before we started storing them. The scheduled daily workflows build true daily history going forward.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "ceaac11f-0c91-420e-bea5-420fff195c3d",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
